0325-negroni-wlan-smmu3-default: Wi-Fi, the 0324 stage-1 context re-checked (negroniwlan_smmu=3, opt-in; default 1 since the 0249 SEA).
SMMU (negroni_wlan_smmu.c rewritten): context bank by the U-Boot qcom-hyp-smmu.c rule (CBAR S2_TRANS, or
S1_TRANS_S2_BYPASS with VMID 0xff) + SCTLR.M off + no valid S2CR into it; CBAR S1_TRANS_S2_BYPASS VMID 0, CBA2R
VA64, TCR/TCR2/MAIR, SCTLR with Android's fault attributes (HUPCF, no CFRE, no stall); S2CR then SMR; every write
read back; SMR 0x1c00 mask 1 (or reuse of an SMR that matches 0x1c01); old CBAR/CBA2R/SMR/S2CR restored on the
failure path; fault line with FSR/FAR/FSYNR0/FSYNR1/CBFRSYNRA + sGFSR/sGFSYNR0-2 decoded (heartbeats, each level,
failure); unmap. Chain (negroni_wlan.c, _mhi.c, _bhi.c, _qmi.c): PCIe BDF-to-SID table programmed like pci-msm.c
(BDF 0x100 -> SID 0x1c01), ASPM off on both ends for the download (ath11k), MHI CTRL/DATA window = the IOVA window
(cnss2), no physical address with policy 3, firmware segments unmapped before free. Writes the apps SMMU and the
PCIe PARF SID table: owner-approved. Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0325".

