 /*
- * NEGRONI QCA6490 Wi-Fi (patch 0324): an apps-SMMU stage-1 context for the WLAN PCIe stream 0x1c01, opt-in
- * with boot-arg negroniwlan_smmu=3.
+ * NEGRONI QCA6490 Wi-Fi (patches 0324, 0325): an apps-SMMU stage-1 context for the WLAN PCIe stream.
+ * Opt-in with negroniwlan_smmu=3 (the default is 1 again: a 0249 boot showed Gunyah refusing a GR1 CBAR write).
  *
  * Why: XNU's RAM starts at 0x840000000, so every buffer the 0261-0323 code gives the chip is above 4 GiB.
- * Android gives this chip IOVAs from 0xa0000000 + 256 MiB (out/live.dts:20856 qcom,iommu-dma-addr-pool, SMMU
- * S1 "fastmap"), Linux ath11k a 32-bit coherent mask (pci.c:24); nobody has shown the QCA6490 firmware uses
- * address bits 32-35 (docs/audit/2026-10-26-wifi.md section 2.1). With negroniwlan_smmu=3 the chip sees the
- * same window as on Android: each host buffer is mapped page by page at the next free IOVA from 0xa0000000,
- * and the stream goes through a translation context we own. Without the boot-arg nothing here runs.
+ * Android gives this chip IOVAs from 0xa0000000 + 256 MiB (out/live.dts cnss_pci_iommu_group:
+ * qcom,iommu-dma-addr-pool, qcom,iommu-dma = "fastmap", qcom,iommu-pagetable = "coherent", qcom,iommu-faults =
+ * "stall-disable", "HUPCF", "no-CFRE", "non-fatal"). The hypervisor (Gunyah) turns an S2CR BYPASS into FAULT
+ * (Linux arm-smmu-qcom.c bypass quirk, U-Boot qcom-hyp-smmu.c), so the only way for the chip to reach RAM is a
+ * translation context. Each host buffer is mapped page by page at the next free IOVA from 0xa0000000.
  *
- * How (Linux arm-smmu.c / io-pgtable-arm.c order, as the GPU code of patch 0233 in negroni_adreno.c does it
- * on the adreno SMMU of this SoC): a context bank nobody uses (SCTLR.M = 0, no S2CR translates into it), its
- * own 3-level 4 KiB page tables (39-bit input, 36-bit output), MAIR/TCR/TTBR0, TLB invalidate + sync, SCTLR
- * on, then S2CR -> the context and the SMR for stream 0x1c01 (an SMR that already matches the stream is
- * reused and restored on the failure path). Every write is read back: the hypervisor (Gunyah) emulates the
- * global space and may refuse it; then the step stops before any DMA. UNTESTED ON HARDWARE.
+ * Stream: PCIe0 has qcom,smmu-sid-base 0x1c00 and iommu-map RID 0x100 -> 0x1c01 (RID 0 -> 0x1c00). The PCIe
+ * controller makes the SID from its BDF-to-SID table (pci-msm.c msm_pcie_config_sid), which the survey's core
+ * reset clears; negroni_wlan.c programs it again (0325). The SMR covers 0x1c00 and 0x1c01 (mask 1) when no
+ * other SMR covers either, so a table that did not take still matches.
+ *
+ * Context bank choice (U-Boot qcom-hyp-smmu.c alloc_cb + Linux arm-smmu.c): CBAR type S2_TRANS, or
+ * S1_TRANS_S2_BYPASS with VMID 0xff (unused); and SCTLR.M = 0; and no valid SMR whose S2CR translates into it.
+ * Programming (Linux arm_smmu_write_context_bank order): SCTLR 0, CBA2R VA64, CBAR S1_TRANS_S2_BYPASS VMID 0,
+ * TCR2, TCR, TTBR0/1, MAIR0/1, FSR clear, TLBIASID + sync, SCTLR on (M TRE AFE HUPCF ASIDPNE; no CFRE, no CFIE,
+ * CFCFG 0 = no stall: Android's fault attributes), then S2CR -> context, then SMR (arm_smmu_write_sme order).
+ * Every write is read back. Faults: context FSR/FAR/FSYNR0/FSYNR1/CBFRSYNRA and global sGFSR/sGFSYNR0-2
+ * are decoded at every heartbeat, at the end of each level and on the failure path.
+ *
+ * Every access is one plain 32-bit ldr/str (negroni_mmio.h, 0255): Gunyah emulates the global space and
+ * injects a synchronous external abort on a writeback, pair, 64-bit or WZR access. UNTESTED ON HARDWARE.
  */
